From: Andrew Udvare <audvare@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Restore basicsr/__init__.py so the package can be installed

Every directory under basicsr/ has an __init__.py except basicsr/ itself,
which this fork dropped; upstream BasicSR still ships one. setup.py calls
find_packages(), which only descends into regular packages, so it returns an
empty list and the built wheel contains nothing but metadata.

Upstream only ever runs "setup.py develop" from a checkout, where basicsr is
picked up as a PEP 420 namespace package from the current directory, so this
never showed up for them.

diff --git a/basicsr/__init__.py b/basicsr/__init__.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e69de29
